1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
"Echo Of A Letter"
(Episode 14)

2
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:27,040
Wait here for me.

3
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,120
I'll go in alone.

4
00:00:29,199 --> 00:00:30,360
Okay.

5
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:31,560
Call me if anything happens.

6
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,280
Let go!

7
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:44,320
The master said

8
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,400
this would be mine.

9
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,480
How come I didn't hear him say that?

10
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,279
Now we listen to the First Madam.

11
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:49,879
It's mine.

12
00:01:49,959 --> 00:01:51,000
It's mine!

13
00:02:01,719 --> 00:02:02,600
Who's there?

14
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:03,320
Mom.

15
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,239
It's me.

16
00:02:04,319 --> 00:02:05,319
Sweetheart.

17
00:02:29,879 --> 00:02:31,240
What are your plans now?

18
00:02:32,439 --> 00:02:34,039
I'll move to Hong Kong first.

19
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,000
After a while,

20
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,919
I'm traveling with friends for a bit.

21
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:39,200
Okay.

22
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,400
Stay safe, then.

23
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,480
If you run short on money,

24
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,560
just tell me.

25
00:02:45,759 --> 00:02:47,439
Didn't you hire someone to watch over me?

26
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,400
Do you blame me?

27
00:02:51,439 --> 00:02:52,680
How dare I blame you?

28
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:54,639
You're all grown up.

29
00:02:54,719 --> 00:02:55,895
You're standing on your own two feet.

30
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:57,280
I can't control you anymore.

31
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:00,800
Then don't worry about me.

32
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:02,959
Right now,

33
00:03:03,039 --> 00:03:04,039
you're free.

34
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,400
Go live a good life for yourself.

35
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:09,800
I know.

36
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,120
I'll get going, then.

37
00:03:19,879 --> 00:03:20,879
Sweetheart.

38
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:51,560
Didn't you say

39
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,719
you wouldn't repeat my mistakes?

40
00:03:56,159 --> 00:03:57,439
They're all the same.

41
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,600
Not a single one of them is reliable.

42
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,800
No.

43
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,840
He's different.

44
00:04:04,039 --> 00:04:05,039
Besides,

45
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,319
I can take responsibility for my own life.

46
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,560
I hope you can too.

47
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,480
All right.

48
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,600
All right, sweetheart.

49
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,879
Don't worry about me.

50
00:04:36,959 --> 00:04:39,000
Your mom knows how to move on.

51
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,360
Okay.

52
00:04:59,279 --> 00:05:00,279
Okay, okay, go on.

53
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:03,399
Okay.

54
00:05:04,439 --> 00:05:05,439
Goodbye.

55
00:05:29,199 --> 00:05:30,480
This ring

56
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:33,079
was a gift from my sweetheart.

57
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,600
Zhao Shengge.

58
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,080
Let's go.

59
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,160
Let's go.

60
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,359
Put together a report

61
00:06:21,439 --> 00:06:22,720
on what we covered today.

62
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:23,976
We'll discuss it at a later meeting.

63
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,600
Let's aim to move the project forward
at the next meeting.

64
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,319
Hopefully things go
smoother for us this time.

65
00:06:31,439 --> 00:06:32,439
Okay.

66
00:06:58,879 --> 00:06:59,879
Bye.

67
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,960
How long have you been waiting?

68
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,040
Not long.

69
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,720
Let's go.

70
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:22,559
No one has ever

71
00:07:22,639 --> 00:07:23,879
waited to take me home before.

72
00:07:27,319 --> 00:07:28,319
Zhao Shengge.

73
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,759
Have a bite first.

74
00:07:37,319 --> 00:07:38,319
Here.

75
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,680
A buttered pineapple bun
from Firecracker Factory.

76
00:07:42,759 --> 00:07:44,439
How did you know I love this place?

77
00:07:44,519 --> 00:07:45,519
I haven't had it in ages.

78
00:07:46,079 --> 00:07:47,600
I know just as much about you

79
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,280
as you know about me.

80
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,399
Though someday,

81
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,920
I'll know even more than you do.

82
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:56,800
What's the plan for tonight?

83
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,920
Let's eat first.

84
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,680
After we finish, I'll take you somewhere.

85
00:08:16,066 --> 00:08:17,973
[Xiaolanshan]

86
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,319
If you mind,

87
00:08:25,399 --> 00:08:26,759
I can turn around right away.

88
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
I don't mind.

89
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,080
Okay.

90
00:08:50,159 --> 00:08:51,159
Boss.

91
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,480
Let's head inside.

92
00:09:13,759 --> 00:09:15,600
Xiaolanshan doesn't seem much different

93
00:09:16,159 --> 00:09:17,480
from sixteen years ago.

94
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,240
It was converted into a sanatorium.

95
00:09:27,759 --> 00:09:28,919
I arranged things in advance.

96
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,640
No one else will come around.

97
00:09:31,159 --> 00:09:32,159
I'm fine.

98
00:09:32,799 --> 00:09:33,960
Besides, you're here with me.

99
00:10:04,399 --> 00:10:06,279
I think this was my old ward.

100
00:10:12,679 --> 00:10:13,920
Room 407.

101
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:14,839
Chen Wan,

102
00:10:14,919 --> 00:10:16,079
take your medicine.

103
00:10:16,159 --> 00:10:17,439
Up his dose of mood stabilizers.

104
00:10:17,519 --> 00:10:18,799
Don't let him cause any trouble.

105
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,840
Zhao Shengge.

106
00:10:24,039 --> 00:10:25,439
For everything you went through,

107
00:10:25,519 --> 00:10:26,960
there needs to be closure.

108
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,360
Zhao Shengge!

109
00:10:38,399 --> 00:10:39,880
What right do you have to lock me up?

110
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:40,976
Taking the law into your own hands?

111
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,279
This is illegal!

112
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:01,679
Zhao Shengge,

113
00:11:01,759 --> 00:11:04,599
I never pegged you for a hopeless romantic.

114
00:11:04,679 --> 00:11:07,240
Going through all this
trouble to drag me here,

115
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,399
all just for him?

116
00:11:13,279 --> 00:11:14,479
Don't let him fool you.

117
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:15,839
He's using you!

118
00:11:15,919 --> 00:11:17,079
He's just like his mother,

119
00:11:17,159 --> 00:11:18,559
selling himself

120
00:11:18,639 --> 00:11:20,439
just to toy with your feelings.

121
00:11:20,519 --> 00:11:23,480
I can't believe you'd fall
for someone so tainted.

122
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,360
Did you know

123
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,280
that back when he was
a kid, he was already...

124
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:40,480
I know.

125
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:44,159
That's the exact reason you're here today.

126
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,519
Also, you've got it wrong.

127
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,039
I pursued him.

128
00:11:50,759 --> 00:11:52,720
I was the one begging him to be with me.

129
00:11:59,679 --> 00:12:01,080
Which hand did he touch you with?

130
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:03,720
His right hand.

131
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,080
Though sixteen years ago,

132
00:12:06,919 --> 00:12:08,679
I already ruined that hand.

133
00:12:11,059 --> 00:12:12,699
Then leave the rest to someone else.

134
00:12:13,159 --> 00:12:14,200
Don't dirty your hands.

135
00:12:19,559 --> 00:12:21,080
His tongue and right hand...

136
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:23,200
I'll have them mailed to his sister.

137
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,280
Chen Bingxin is right next door.

138
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Want to see him?

139
00:12:38,919 --> 00:12:39,919
No need.

140
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:43,520
I heard Chen Bingxin had
a sudden brain hemorrhage

141
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,879
and was sent to a sanatorium.

142
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,759
Isn't this a sanatorium?

143
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:08,799
Sixteen years ago,

144
00:13:08,879 --> 00:13:10,399
this is where we met.

145
00:13:11,679 --> 00:13:14,080
Tonight's moon is the
same as sixteen years ago.

146
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,360
Yet a little different, too.

147
00:13:17,759 --> 00:13:18,759
Yes.

148
00:13:21,399 --> 00:13:22,399
Zhao Shengge.

149
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:29,639
None of what Liao Quan said is true.

150
00:13:31,759 --> 00:13:32,840
What I said is true.

151
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,120
Every single word.

152
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,680
Though I think there's one thing
he didn't lie to me about.

153
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,360
You played me.

154
00:13:45,519 --> 00:13:46,879
You said you liked me,

155
00:13:48,039 --> 00:13:49,559
yet had no intention of pursuing me.

156
00:13:50,399 --> 00:13:51,479
While pursuing me,

157
00:13:51,559 --> 00:13:53,120
you were already planning your way out.

158
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:55,999
You said we should be together,

159
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,440
yet never planned on
staying together for long.

160
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,639
I don't think he was slandering you at all.

161
00:14:08,279 --> 00:14:09,279
I wasn't.

162
00:14:10,919 --> 00:14:11,919
You better not be.

163
00:14:58,559 --> 00:14:59,600
Did I wake you?

164
00:15:00,879 --> 00:15:01,879
Where are you going?

165
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,479
To take some medicine.

166
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:05,559
I can't sleep.

167
00:15:06,279 --> 00:15:07,400
Monica prescribed me

168
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:09,360
a low-dose sleep aid.

169
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:11,120
Taking it might help me fall asleep.

170
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,559
Then don't try to sleep.

171
00:15:19,559 --> 00:15:20,559
Where are we going?

172
00:15:21,679 --> 00:15:23,199
Let's sit in the living room together.

173
00:15:39,919 --> 00:15:40,959
Thank you.

174
00:15:41,039 --> 00:15:43,320
Let's pay Monica another visit tomorrow.

175
00:15:45,759 --> 00:15:46,759
Okay.

176
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,919
Is it because we went
to Xiaolanshan tonight?

177
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:52,559
No.

178
00:15:52,639 --> 00:15:54,600
It's because I started
thinking about my mom.

179
00:15:55,559 --> 00:15:57,320
It must have been many years ago.

180
00:15:57,879 --> 00:15:59,959
Back when I was still
living in the tenement.

181
00:16:00,039 --> 00:16:01,240
One time,

182
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,199
a bunch of kids beat me up.

183
00:16:03,279 --> 00:16:04,360
I was badly hurt

184
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,120
and came down with a
high fever when I got back.

185
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:09,399
Back then, she

186
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,800
stole a piece of jewelry
from the Chen family

187
00:16:12,519 --> 00:16:14,679
and pawned it to pay for my treatment.

188
00:16:14,759 --> 00:16:16,200
She even bought me a bag of candy.

189
00:16:23,799 --> 00:16:25,320
I only found out later

190
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:27,679
that she was beaten after she went back.

191
00:16:28,919 --> 00:16:30,600
Chen Bingxin beat her,

192
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,760
and the First Madam, who ran the finances,
beat her again.

193
00:16:34,919 --> 00:16:36,280
When I found out,

194
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,919
I was heartbroken and furious.

195
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:39,599
I hated

196
00:16:39,679 --> 00:16:41,080
how useless I was.

197
00:16:42,399 --> 00:16:44,279
Yet I didn't dare let her know.

198
00:16:46,039 --> 00:16:47,080
You were just a child.

199
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,840
You might not believe me,

200
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:52,679
but before I met you,

201
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:56,360
I wanted to kill Chen
Bingxin several times.

202
00:16:58,519 --> 00:17:01,399
I never even told Zhuo Zhixuan about this.

203
00:17:02,039 --> 00:17:04,079
Though he eventually picked up on it,

204
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:07,440
so he took me to see Monica.

205
00:17:08,759 --> 00:17:10,680
He's gotten what he deserved now.

206
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:14,920
What else?

207
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:18,640
Also, around the time
I got into your school,

208
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:19,720
she went to a casino.

209
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,160
After Chen Bingxin found out,

210
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,240
he locked both of us in the basement.

211
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:33,000
I didn't know

212
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,559
she went to the casino

213
00:17:36,519 --> 00:17:39,000
so I could afford to study abroad.

214
00:17:39,839 --> 00:17:40,839
I didn't dare ask.

215
00:17:42,079 --> 00:17:43,519
I was afraid she'd say yes,

216
00:17:44,519 --> 00:17:46,160
and just as afraid she'd say no.

217
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:51,279
After she bought my way out of Xiaolanshan,

218
00:17:52,319 --> 00:17:54,599
she didn't have a penny left to her name.

219
00:17:55,599 --> 00:17:57,599
For someone who cared
so much about her looks,

220
00:17:59,559 --> 00:18:02,079
during my first year out of Xiaolanshan,

221
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:05,079
she didn't wear a single piece of jewelry.

222
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:07,599
Maybe that's why.

223
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:12,080
I later developed a habit
of collecting gemstones.

224
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:14,519
She wanted me to fight
for shares in Rongxin.

225
00:18:14,599 --> 00:18:16,880
Thinking back on it, she wasn't wrong.

226
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:21,720
All of her shares went
toward getting me out.

227
00:18:22,759 --> 00:18:24,559
I owed her that to begin with.

228
00:18:25,759 --> 00:18:27,160
So that's why.

229
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:31,279
She used to be a wonderful mom.

230
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:34,799
I really loved her.

231
00:18:37,359 --> 00:18:38,359
It's just...

232
00:18:40,319 --> 00:18:42,119
reality was too cruel.

233
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,400
It's okay.

234
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,040
I'm having people watch over her for you.

235
00:18:48,799 --> 00:18:50,079
She'll be fine.

236
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,600
If you ever want to,

237
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:54,079
you can see her anytime.

238
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:56,640
No need.

239
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,519
Let nature take its course.

240
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,079
Things like this can't be forced.

241
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,480
It's for the best this way.

242
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,840
Monica said

243
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:10,720
the biggest issue is wanting
to control everything.

244
00:19:11,599 --> 00:19:12,599
Letting go

245
00:19:14,039 --> 00:19:15,039
will be better.

246
00:19:18,359 --> 00:19:19,359
Chen Wan.

247
00:19:20,359 --> 00:19:22,160
You can lean on me a little more.

248
00:19:28,599 --> 00:19:29,599
Zhao Shengge,

249
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:34,319
you don't actually hate dogs, right?

250
00:19:36,799 --> 00:19:39,079
I saw it last time I
went to the Chen house.

251
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,079
I don't hate dogs.

252
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:46,400
When I was young, I
raised one just like it,

253
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,400
until someone got rid of it.

254
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:52,759
Should we get another one?

255
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,160
Just like the one we saw

256
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:58,039
by the roadside last time.

257
00:19:58,119 --> 00:19:59,439
Tiny,

258
00:19:59,519 --> 00:20:00,920
with a little round head.

259
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,560
I'm not scared of that kind.

260
00:20:03,119 --> 00:20:05,759
We could take it swimming with us,

261
00:20:05,839 --> 00:20:07,999
go see the view at Victoria Harbour,

262
00:20:08,079 --> 00:20:09,440
and visit Victoria Peak.

263
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,039
While you swim,

264
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:16,000
the two of us can time you together.

265
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:19,880
No need to get one.

266
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,079
I already have one.

267
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:27,959
Okay.

268
00:20:28,039 --> 00:20:29,039
Zhao Shengge.

269
00:20:29,759 --> 00:20:30,759
I'd love to.

270
00:20:42,519 --> 00:20:43,519
Chen Wan.

271
00:20:44,839 --> 00:20:45,880
Thank you for everything.

272
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:02,160
I already told him not to buy
such expensive clothes.

273
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,199
Money should be spent on research.

274
00:21:05,279 --> 00:21:07,199
Zhao Shengge never
listens no matter what I say.

275
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:08,959
All right, Dr. Fang.

276
00:21:09,039 --> 00:21:10,959
You're getting your research funding too.

277
00:21:11,039 --> 00:21:12,335
I told you to keep the price a secret,

278
00:21:12,359 --> 00:21:13,519
and you didn't listen either.

279
00:21:14,359 --> 00:21:15,960
Xu Zhiying let it slip.

280
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:18,015
She recently fought her two brothers

281
00:21:18,039 --> 00:21:19,519
for power in the family

282
00:21:19,599 --> 00:21:20,679
and won.

283
00:21:20,759 --> 00:21:21,839
She was in too good a mood.

284
00:21:23,319 --> 00:21:24,319
Chen Wan.

285
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,136
How did you know that when I returned home,

286
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:28,160
I'd be at Exit B3?

287
00:21:30,079 --> 00:21:32,999
Just how thoroughly did
Zhuo Zhixuan sell me out?

288
00:21:33,079 --> 00:21:34,839
I didn't even have to
bribe or threaten him.

289
00:21:35,799 --> 00:21:38,200
Guess your rock-solid friendship
isn't all that strong.

290
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,039
Actually, it's pretty simple.

291
00:21:41,839 --> 00:21:43,920
I have a friend over
there I worked with before.

292
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,120
Even without exact details,

293
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:48,000
I could make a rough guess.

294
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:49,720
That smart, huh?

295
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,199
Yeah.

296
00:21:51,279 --> 00:21:52,479
And that wasn't the only time.

297
00:21:52,559 --> 00:21:53,719
There was another time.

298
00:21:53,799 --> 00:21:55,720
Remember when you were attacked in Italy?

299
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,440
You have no idea

300
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,959
how unreliable Haishi's paparazzi are.

301
00:22:00,039 --> 00:22:03,759
Sensationalized headlines, twisted facts,
and blurred truths.

302
00:22:03,839 --> 00:22:06,880
One minute they said you were
in critical condition,

303
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:09,920
the next they said you were shot in
the chest and needed an amputation.

304
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,656
You have no idea how
worried I was about you.

305
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:13,319
I only hurt my hand.

306
00:22:13,839 --> 00:22:14,360
Though Minglong

307
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:16,519
squashed the story pretty quickly,

308
00:22:16,599 --> 00:22:18,360
and the paparazzi
never brought it up again.

309
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,999
If I hadn't been applying for a visa

310
00:22:20,079 --> 00:22:22,640
when Zhuo Zhixuan told me
you were safe,

311
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,600
I really would've flown right over.

312
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,319
Those tabloids really are unreliable.

313
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,760
Whether Haishi's paparazzi are reliable

314
00:22:28,839 --> 00:22:30,160
on other stories, I don't know.

315
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,999
When it comes to reporting
on you two, though,

316
00:22:33,079 --> 00:22:34,599
they actually got some of it right.

317
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:37,320
Like, "Young Heir Falls
in Love at Repulse Bay,".

318
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,479
"Secret Three-Day Tryst with Close Friend,"

319
00:22:39,559 --> 00:22:41,600
and "Zhao Heir Turns Charitable,

320
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,839
Handing Out Water to Paparazzi."

321
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:46,080
Even my mom asked me

322
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,559
if you two are actually an item.

323
00:22:48,559 --> 00:22:50,479
Her mahjong buddies know we work together,

324
00:22:50,559 --> 00:22:51,856
and they're all dying of curiosity.

325
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:53,600
Mrs. Xu reads that stuff too?

326
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:54,719
All right, all right.

327
00:22:54,799 --> 00:22:56,679
Stop chatting about nonsense.

328
00:22:56,759 --> 00:22:59,239
Now, about controlling these metrics,

329
00:22:59,319 --> 00:23:01,160
I need to go over it
clearly with you again.

330
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:03,800
Those eco-warriors will
definitely latch onto this.

331
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:06,279
Your flight is about to depart.

332
00:23:06,359 --> 00:23:07,840
We wish you a pleasant journey.

333
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:08,679
Look at this...

334
00:23:08,759 --> 00:23:09,479
All right, Dr. Fang.

335
00:23:09,559 --> 00:23:10,400
Let's talk once we're on the plane.

336
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,120
Okay.

337
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:12,400
We'll talk on the plane, then.

338
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,920
This is very important.

339
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:18,680
By the way,

340
00:23:20,759 --> 00:23:21,759
back when I graduated,

341
00:23:22,839 --> 00:23:24,599
I boarded from that gate right up ahead.

342
00:23:25,559 --> 00:23:26,880
I knew Zhuo Zhixuan sold me out,

343
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:28,880
just didn't expect him
to do it this thoroughly.

344
00:23:30,839 --> 00:23:32,239
Then from now on, I'll see you off.

345
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,720
Okay.

346
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:44,600
Are you sure you won't go onstage?

347
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:47,400
Make sure you remember

348
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,440
the points on environmental metrics.

349
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,999
Who knows what they'll ask later.

350
00:23:52,079 --> 00:23:53,560
Don't worry, Dr. Fang.

351
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,039
I'm unstoppable right now.

352
00:23:55,119 --> 00:23:57,680
Nothing's getting in my way.

353
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:00,400
All right.

354
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:04,600
Nervous?

355
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:06,279
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't.

356
00:24:06,359 --> 00:24:08,320
It's my first roadshow with you.

357
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,400
Still,

358
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:10,960
we've got this.

359
00:24:15,039 --> 00:24:16,039
You got this.

360
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,199
Welcome, investors
and guests.

361
00:24:20,278 --> 00:24:22,919
Please, welcome our presenter today,

362
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,880
Ms. Xu Zhiying,

363
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:26,960
Mr. Fang Jian, and Mr. Chen Wan.

364
00:24:28,799 --> 00:24:30,535
Led by renowned Haishi
enterprise Minglong Group,

365
00:24:30,559 --> 00:24:33,239
the Lai Chi Wun Project investment roadshow

366
00:24:33,319 --> 00:24:34,519
has officially kicked off.

367
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:36,833
Spanning 23 cities worldwide,
this roadshow event

368
00:24:36,893 --> 00:24:38,079
[Exclusive News Report: Project Reactors Xu
Zhiying, Fang Jian and Chen Wan appear present]

369
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,439
aims to build a collaborative,

370
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:41,640
mutually beneficial port ecosystem.

371
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:43,080
Project leads Xu Zhiying,

372
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:45,679
Fang Jian, and Chen Wan
appeared at the roadshow.

373
00:24:45,738 --> 00:24:48,178
Among the Lai Chi Wun leadership team,

374
00:24:48,279 --> 00:24:50,080
a fresh East Asian face

375
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:52,120
made his debut before investors.

376
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:54,439
This young executive, Chen Wan,

377
00:24:54,519 --> 00:24:55,959
has drawn widespread attention.

378
00:24:56,039 --> 00:24:58,199
What the Lai Chi Wun Project brings us

379
00:24:58,279 --> 00:24:59,880
is more than just an equipment upgrade—

380
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:03,320
it is a complete paradigm
shift in technology.

381
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:06,120
The Lai Chi Wun Project
attracts diverse industries,

382
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,759
forming a major
industrial hub in the future.

383
00:25:09,839 --> 00:25:11,880
In constructing the
offshore oil support tunnel,

384
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:14,479
we adopted eight different
power technologies,

385
00:25:14,559 --> 00:25:16,400
not only reducing risks,

386
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:18,160
while also greatly improving efficiency.

387
00:25:20,119 --> 00:25:20,959
Yes, you.

388
00:25:21,039 --> 00:25:22,080
Ms. Xu,

389
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:24,880
how do you balance your marriage life

390
00:25:24,979 --> 00:25:26,899
and your carrier in the future?

391
00:25:29,039 --> 00:25:30,920
May I ask you, sir,

392
00:25:31,599 --> 00:25:32,679
did you get press access

393
00:25:32,759 --> 00:25:34,759
to our Lai Chi Wun Project roadshow

394
00:25:34,839 --> 00:25:36,120
through your connections

395
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:38,319
at The Wall Street Journal?

396
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:40,880
Excuse me,

397
00:25:40,960 --> 00:25:43,120
as head of PR for the Lai Chi Wun Project,

398
00:25:43,213 --> 00:25:45,933
staying well-informed is part of my job.

399
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:46,759
Then, Ms. Xu,

400
00:25:46,845 --> 00:25:48,886
how do you plan to balance

401
00:25:48,939 --> 00:25:52,458
your future and your career and marriage?

402
00:25:52,559 --> 00:25:53,840
Tell me please.

403
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:54,719
I think

404
00:25:54,799 --> 00:25:56,519
asking that question at an event like this

405
00:25:56,599 --> 00:25:57,759
is completely unprofessional.

406
00:25:58,599 --> 00:25:59,719
Next question.

407
00:25:59,799 --> 00:26:01,840
Does anyone have a question?

408
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:02,959
Yes, you.

409
00:26:03,039 --> 00:26:03,840
Mr. Chen Wan.

410
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:04,840
As far as I know,

411
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:07,039
deep-sea survey technology
for complex environments

412
00:26:07,119 --> 00:26:09,239
has already seen
breakthroughs in Country A.

413
00:26:09,319 --> 00:26:10,535
What advantages does Minglong's technology

414
00:26:10,559 --> 00:26:12,279
hold over Country A's?

415
00:26:12,359 --> 00:26:14,679
And what impact will this project have

416
00:26:14,759 --> 00:26:16,519
on marine ecology and
neighboring countries?

417
00:26:16,559 --> 00:26:17,616
This question is too sensitive.

418
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:19,559
Should we check with upper management?

419
00:26:20,519 --> 00:26:21,840
It's fine.

420
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:23,759
Thank you for your question.

421
00:26:23,839 --> 00:26:25,360
The technology you mentioned—

422
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,800
I've heard a bit about it.

423
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:28,039
Unfortunately, though,

424
00:26:28,119 --> 00:26:29,400
at present, that technology

425
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:31,759
remains strictly in the laboratory stage.

426
00:26:31,839 --> 00:26:33,719
Our domestic deep-sea
exploration technology

427
00:26:33,799 --> 00:26:35,840
was the first to overcome
challenges in high-low

428
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:38,199
dynamic positioning
float-over installations.

429
00:26:38,279 --> 00:26:39,999
Both our modular construction technology

430
00:26:40,079 --> 00:26:41,120
and subsea operations

431
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:43,199
have fully entered the ultra-deepwater era.

432
00:26:43,279 --> 00:26:45,880
Our all-weather, all-sea
float-over capability,

433
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:48,080
operational difficulty,
and technical complexity

434
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:49,416
have topped international rankings

435
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:50,679
for ten consecutive years,

436
00:26:50,759 --> 00:26:52,640
and are already in active use.

437
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:55,216
In recent years, we've partnered closely with
several marine conservation member nations,

438
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:56,759
carrying out in-depth cooperation

439
00:26:56,839 --> 00:26:58,279
with remarkable results.

440
00:26:58,359 --> 00:27:00,800
These achievements
are evident to all nations,

441
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:02,759
so please don't misattribute the credit.

442
00:27:02,839 --> 00:27:04,015
As for the Lai Chi Wun Project,

443
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:05,039
it is not only a catalyst

444
00:27:05,119 --> 00:27:07,559
for advancing marine
science and technology,

445
00:27:08,079 --> 00:27:09,479
it is also

446
00:27:09,559 --> 00:27:10,479
a driving force in protecting

447
00:27:10,559 --> 00:27:12,560
our marine ecological barrier,

448
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:15,920
and a bridge for Asia-Pacific
economic cooperation.

449
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:17,039
This is

450
00:27:17,119 --> 00:27:18,199
the Lai Chi Wun Project's

451
00:27:18,279 --> 00:27:20,160
unwavering social responsibility,

452
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,360
as well as

453
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:22,999
our R&amp;D team's

454
00:27:23,079 --> 00:27:24,519
steadfast goal.

455
00:27:25,359 --> 00:27:26,359
Thank you.

456
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:37,279
Today,

457
00:27:37,359 --> 00:27:38,840
we are ushering in

458
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,840
a new era of smart meteorology.

459
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:43,080
With the development
of oil-monitoring robots,

460
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:45,560
every effort is better secured,

461
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:48,440
and every life can be better protected.

462
00:27:49,559 --> 00:27:51,999
Now I've actually made it to his side.

463
00:27:52,079 --> 00:27:54,959
The flowers and applause
I never got in my youth—

464
00:27:55,039 --> 00:27:57,160
Zhao Shengge made up for all of them.

465
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:05,200
Dr. Fang,

466
00:28:05,799 --> 00:28:07,120
regarding the upcoming project,

467
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:08,480
I need to follow up with you.

468
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,640
Congratulations.

469
00:28:11,799 --> 00:28:12,839
Thanks for your hard work.

470
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:19,119
Did you pick these flowers?

471
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:21,319
You copied me.

472
00:28:21,839 --> 00:28:23,120
I thought you'd like them.

473
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,360
Zhao Shengge,

474
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:25,560
let me tell you a secret

475
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:27,160
that not even Zhuo Zhixuan knows.

476
00:28:27,839 --> 00:28:28,759
Back in junior year of high school,

477
00:28:28,839 --> 00:28:30,679
when you broke the swimming record,

478
00:28:30,759 --> 00:28:32,360
I sent you a bouquet of flowers.

479
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:33,800
I didn't mean anything else by it.

480
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:36,400
I simply wanted to congratulate you.

481
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:39,479
White peonies stand for sincerity,

482
00:28:39,559 --> 00:28:41,319
and pink hydrangeas stand for fulfillment.

483
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:44,719
I hoped that no matter what you did,

484
00:28:44,799 --> 00:28:46,519
it would be successful and fulfilling.

485
00:28:48,079 --> 00:28:48,640
Back then, though,

486
00:28:48,720 --> 00:28:50,999
you thought they were from a stranger,

487
00:28:51,079 --> 00:28:53,319
so you casually handed
my flowers to someone else.

488
00:28:56,759 --> 00:28:57,759
I'm sorry.

489
00:28:58,880 --> 00:29:00,199
It's okay.

490
00:29:00,279 --> 00:29:01,720
I've already gotten my flowers.

491
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:03,680
Let's go.

492
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:16,640
It's snowing.

493
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,600
Let's go take a look.

494
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:19,239
Come on.

495
00:29:19,319 --> 00:29:21,199
At the Lai Chi Wun Project Roadshow,

496
00:29:21,279 --> 00:29:23,640
Project Lead Chen Wan Shines Bright.

497
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,519
Lai Chi Wun Project CTO Chen Wan:

498
00:29:26,599 --> 00:29:27,896
Honed In and Deepened by Past Experience.

499
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:29,200
The snow is coming down so hard.

500
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,360
Careful not to catch a chill.

501
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:36,480
Look.

502
00:29:37,319 --> 00:29:40,640
That's where you attended
your first press conference

503
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:42,079
for a cross-border acquisition.

504
00:29:44,119 --> 00:29:45,439
Look at that hall.

505
00:29:45,519 --> 00:29:46,519
That hall

506
00:29:46,599 --> 00:29:49,320
is where reporters secretly
photographed you for the first time.

507
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,279
Really?

508
00:29:50,359 --> 00:29:51,279
Yeah.

509
00:29:51,359 --> 00:29:53,320
I think it was when I attended that year's.

510
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:55,400
Pacific Rim Economic Cooperation Forum.

511
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:57,880
Then...

512
00:29:58,559 --> 00:30:00,319
what were you doing around that time?

513
00:30:01,799 --> 00:30:02,799
Me?

514
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,295
I was subtly fishing for news about you

515
00:30:05,319 --> 00:30:07,319
from Zhuo Zhixuan,

516
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,479
and constantly studying

517
00:30:09,559 --> 00:30:11,039
finance and economics,

518
00:30:11,119 --> 00:30:12,960
planning to found Kexiang.

519
00:30:15,193 --> 00:30:16,193
That time in your life—

520
00:30:16,839 --> 00:30:18,400
I've already missed out on it forever.

521
00:30:41,559 --> 00:30:43,160
I don't want to miss out anymore.

522
00:30:45,039 --> 00:30:46,039
All right.

523
00:30:55,799 --> 00:30:57,080
Chen Wan,

524
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:58,359
I have something for you.

525
00:30:59,359 --> 00:31:00,359
What is it?

526
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:09,960
Take a look.

527
00:31:11,039 --> 00:31:13,439
This isn't to celebrate
your successful roadshow.

528
00:31:13,519 --> 00:31:15,495
Actually, I've wanted to give
this to you for a long time,

529
00:31:15,519 --> 00:31:17,176
but it got delayed for
quite a while recently.

530
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:19,240
Haishi Homeless Children Foundation.

531
00:31:20,119 --> 00:31:20,999
If I remember right,

532
00:31:21,079 --> 00:31:23,079
after Haishi's new financial
regulations came out,

533
00:31:23,119 --> 00:31:24,775
setting up a foundation
became really difficult.

534
00:31:24,799 --> 00:31:25,160
How did you...

535
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:26,120
That day,

536
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:27,519
outside the shooting club,

537
00:31:27,599 --> 00:31:29,015
you helped that little boy pick up bottles.

538
00:31:29,039 --> 00:31:30,039
I saw it.

539
00:31:30,839 --> 00:31:32,095
You kept sponsoring him after that,

540
00:31:32,119 --> 00:31:33,119
didn't you?

541
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:38,240
Why didn't I see you that day?

542
00:31:38,920 --> 00:31:39,840
Because

543
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:42,733
you were having a great time
chatting with Qin Zhaoting.

544
00:31:44,279 --> 00:31:45,120
Zhao Shengge,

545
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:47,119
you fired a shot toward me that day.

546
00:31:48,359 --> 00:31:49,600
Come to think of it,

547
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:51,240
why did you shoot toward me?

548
00:31:52,279 --> 00:31:53,279
Back then, you...

549
00:31:53,319 --> 00:31:55,399
You just happened to be
standing next to the target.

550
00:31:56,799 --> 00:31:58,176
I wondered for a long time that day

551
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,279
whether you disliked me.

552
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:03,160
I didn't.

553
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:05,360
Don't tell me you
already liked me back then.

554
00:32:05,440 --> 00:32:06,440
That early?

555
00:32:08,839 --> 00:32:09,879
Let me show you something.

556
00:32:18,599 --> 00:32:19,599
Open it and see.

557
00:32:31,759 --> 00:32:33,199
This robot

558
00:32:33,279 --> 00:32:36,039
looks identical to the
one in Shaw Building.

559
00:32:36,839 --> 00:32:37,839
Right?

560
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:40,039
That one was made for the university.

561
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:41,880
This one is specially for you.

562
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:44,400
Though,

563
00:32:45,279 --> 00:32:46,840
even though I'm giving it to you,

564
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:49,560
you can still talk to me whenever
you have something on your mind.

565
00:32:50,720 --> 00:32:52,479
Everything you used to say to it,

566
00:32:52,559 --> 00:32:53,879
you can say to me all over again.

567
00:32:55,839 --> 00:32:56,839
Zhao Shengge,

568
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:59,599
it seems like you really love me.

569
00:33:00,799 --> 00:33:02,200
You're only realizing that now?

570
00:33:08,799 --> 00:33:10,759
I was under a
lot of pressure back then,

571
00:33:11,279 --> 00:33:14,120
and I wasn't really used
to talking to people,

572
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:15,920
so I'd sneak into Shaw Building

573
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,559
to chat with the robot.

574
00:33:18,119 --> 00:33:18,800
Every time after talking to it,

575
00:33:18,880 --> 00:33:20,279
I'd feel so much better.

576
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:23,039
It's been so long now,

577
00:33:23,720 --> 00:33:24,840
I don't even really remember

578
00:33:24,920 --> 00:33:26,200
what I said.

579
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:29,519
Then there's no need to recall it.

580
00:33:31,559 --> 00:33:32,800
Every time I finished talking,

581
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:34,359
my heart would feel much lighter.

582
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:37,160
It was just rough on Zhuo Zhixuan.

583
00:33:37,240 --> 00:33:38,240
You have no idea.

584
00:33:38,279 --> 00:33:41,120
The first time he saw me
chatting with the robot,

585
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:43,400
you wouldn't believe how shocked he looked.

586
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,560
And then he had to pretend

587
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,039
like it was no big deal at all.

588
00:33:46,119 --> 00:33:48,400
You have no idea how
thoughtful he was trying to be.

589
00:34:00,519 --> 00:34:01,759
Thank you.

590
00:34:01,839 --> 00:34:02,839
These gifts—.

591
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,519
I love them all.

592
00:34:05,079 --> 00:34:06,079
No need to thank me.

593
00:34:07,079 --> 00:34:08,479
You'll have to pay me back.

594
00:34:08,559 --> 00:34:09,559
How?

595
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:42,840
Sir,

596
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:43,920
right this way.

597
00:34:46,320 --> 00:34:47,800
We have a gathering today.

598
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:49,760
We shouldn't have
stayed up so late last night.

599
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:52,480
Maybe it would've been earlier
if you'd put the robot down sooner.

600
00:34:53,880 --> 00:34:54,880
By the way, Zhao Shengge,

601
00:34:56,679 --> 00:34:58,559
I just noticed something.

602
00:34:58,639 --> 00:34:59,776
On the cufflinks you gave me,

603
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:02,400
there's a tiny circle on the bottom.

604
00:35:02,480 --> 00:35:03,599
Could you tell me

605
00:35:03,679 --> 00:35:04,679
what it means?

606
00:35:06,039 --> 00:35:06,720
Drop it.

607
00:35:06,800 --> 00:35:08,120
It doesn't mean anything special.

608
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:09,440
Zhao Shengge.

609
00:35:12,880 --> 00:35:13,920
It just means

610
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,239
that you're really stubborn.

611
00:35:17,559 --> 00:35:18,879
Let's go, we're going to be late.

612
00:35:20,039 --> 00:35:20,479
Chen Wan.

613
00:35:20,559 --> 00:35:21,320
Shengge.

614
00:35:21,400 --> 00:35:22,599
Mr. Tan.

615
00:35:22,679 --> 00:35:23,360
Did everything go smoothly?

616
00:35:23,440 --> 00:35:24,679
When did you land?

617
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:26,320
With yesterday's weather,

618
00:35:26,400 --> 00:35:28,639
Shen Zongnian's private
jet was bumpy as hell.

619
00:35:28,719 --> 00:35:29,959
Halfway through my nap,

620
00:35:30,039 --> 00:35:32,055
I thought the plane was doing
somersaults in the troposphere.

621
00:35:32,079 --> 00:35:33,319
The roadshow was a big success.

622
00:35:33,639 --> 00:35:34,079
Congratulations.

623
00:35:34,639 --> 00:35:35,639
Thank you.

624
00:35:35,679 --> 00:35:37,559
It's the result of everyone's hard work.

625
00:35:39,639 --> 00:35:41,320
In this awful Manchester weather,

626
00:35:42,039 --> 00:35:43,175
look at how little you're wearing.

627
00:35:43,199 --> 00:35:45,039
Trying to show off how
cold-resistant you are?

628
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:46,480
What do you know?

629
00:35:46,519 --> 00:35:47,599
It's called fashion.

630
00:35:47,679 --> 00:35:49,400
Look how dashing it makes me.

631
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:50,720
You're the one freezing.

632
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:52,079
Come on, we're late.

633
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:03,320
This banquet hall...

634
00:36:04,199 --> 00:36:05,959
Come, let me introduce
you to a few friends.

635
00:36:29,199 --> 00:36:30,199
How's it going?

636
00:36:31,039 --> 00:36:32,039
Pursuing him.

637
00:36:33,519 --> 00:36:35,720
With a personality like his,

638
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:37,240
I thought once he was in your hands,

639
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:39,495
you'd definitely have him
wrapped around your finger.

640
00:36:39,519 --> 00:36:40,519
Is that so?

641
00:36:42,119 --> 00:36:43,896
The one nursing a crush
and making the first move

642
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:45,679
can stop their feelings anytime.

643
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:47,520
Whereas the one who falls hard

644
00:36:48,519 --> 00:36:49,936
can only do everything in their power

645
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:51,719
to hold on to and ask for that devotion.

646
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:54,320
In this relationship,

647
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:55,639
the one holding the upper hand

648
00:36:56,199 --> 00:36:57,199
has never been me.

649
00:36:59,519 --> 00:37:00,519
You're on the back foot?

650
00:37:01,119 --> 00:37:02,119
What?

651
00:37:03,639 --> 00:37:04,639
Forget it.

652
00:37:05,760 --> 00:37:07,360
There's a lid for every pot.

653
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:09,999
Don't you think?

654
00:37:10,079 --> 00:37:10,880
Chen Wan,

655
00:37:10,960 --> 00:37:12,960
it has a great pleasure to meet you.

656
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:14,959
Just call me Keats.

657
00:37:15,039 --> 00:37:16,360
A little jewelry for you—

658
00:37:16,439 --> 00:37:18,479
just a small token of my fppreciation.

659
00:37:18,559 --> 00:37:19,655
You've come a long way,

660
00:37:19,679 --> 00:37:21,320
these jewels are far too precious.

661
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:22,720
But I accept your kind intent.

662
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:24,519
I have prepared some specialty today.

663
00:37:24,599 --> 00:37:26,599
This gift is small. Just take it.

664
00:37:26,679 --> 00:37:28,760
It's been a great pleasure talking to you.

665
00:37:28,833 --> 00:37:31,152
There will be a music concert between two days.

666
00:37:31,239 --> 00:37:32,440
Will you like to join me?

667
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:34,400
Excuse me,

668
00:37:34,466 --> 00:37:35,065
I just...

669
00:37:35,159 --> 00:37:36,159
Chen Wan.

670
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:38,880
Just a minute.

671
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,400
It's about time.

672
00:37:43,159 --> 00:37:44,159
We can head out now.

673
00:37:45,159 --> 00:37:46,439
What about Ms. Xu and Dr. Fang?

674
00:37:46,519 --> 00:37:47,519
Where did they go?

675
00:37:47,559 --> 00:37:49,279
Fang Jian made a brief appearance and left.

676
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:51,680
Dining gets in the way of
his grand scientific pursuits.

677
00:37:52,159 --> 00:37:53,240
Ms. Xu went back.

678
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:54,360
She's not coming with us.

679
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:55,360
She's going on vacation in Northern Europe.

680
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:56,440
That's nice.

681
00:37:57,800 --> 00:37:58,680
Are you tired?

682
00:37:58,760 --> 00:37:59,800
I'm fine.

683
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:00,880
Let's go.

684
00:38:11,800 --> 00:38:12,976
Is the view from the 72nd floor

685
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:14,680
better than a concert?

686
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,760
Keats.

687
00:38:19,559 --> 00:38:20,240
Zhao Shengge,

688
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:21,639
I didn't agree to go

689
00:38:21,719 --> 00:38:22,760
to the concert with him.

690
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:28,360
I don't know what you're talking about.

691
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:29,679
You can do whatever you want.

692
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:32,159
I won't interfere.

693
00:39:14,159 --> 00:39:15,159
Zhao Shengge,

694
00:39:16,039 --> 00:39:17,719
in the cabinet over there,

695
00:39:18,719 --> 00:39:20,039
on the second shelf,

696
00:39:20,119 --> 00:39:21,119
there's something inside.

697
00:39:21,199 --> 00:39:22,679
Could you go get it for me?

698
00:39:42,119 --> 00:39:43,320
This letter—

699
00:39:43,400 --> 00:39:45,400
everything I've wanted to say to you

700
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:47,280
over the past sixteen years

701
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:48,480
is all in here.

702
00:39:50,639 --> 00:39:51,720
From now on,

703
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:53,639
you don't need to ask Zhuo Zhixuan anymore.

704
00:39:53,719 --> 00:39:55,320
You can just ask me.

705
00:39:56,440 --> 00:39:58,055
Even though I'd really love
to see the look on your face

706
00:39:58,079 --> 00:39:59,400
when you read this letter,

707
00:40:00,039 --> 00:40:01,719
I'm going to take a shower now.

708
00:40:04,239 --> 00:40:05,239
Okay.

709
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:29,240
Zhao.

710
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:30,039
Sheng-

711
00:40:30,119 --> 00:40:31,400
ge.

712
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:33,320
Just writing your name

713
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:35,119
has already taken everything I have.

714
00:40:35,719 --> 00:40:37,880
Your name is an incantation.

715
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:40,599
For someone brimming with secrets,

716
00:40:40,679 --> 00:40:42,280
merely writing it down by hand

717
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:44,719
feels like breaking some taboo.

718
00:40:45,639 --> 00:40:46,920
I don't know if this letter

719
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:48,280
will ever be sent,

720
00:40:49,159 --> 00:40:50,639
just like the countless ones

721
00:40:50,719 --> 00:40:52,000
before it.

722
00:41:02,239 --> 00:41:04,240
A secret crush requires good manners.

723
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:06,639
Unrequited love has its fundamental rules.

724
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:09,599
Perhaps I shouldn't
even write these letters.

725
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:11,360
These thoughts

726
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:13,920
should circle silently within my chest.

727
00:41:14,440 --> 00:41:15,559
There is no reason,

728
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:17,320
nor should you have to bear,

729
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:20,119
any burden because of them.

730
00:41:25,239 --> 00:41:26,400
Mr. Zhao,

731
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:27,679
I hope you always win.

732
00:41:28,199 --> 00:41:29,599
I wish you good fortune.

733
00:41:29,679 --> 00:41:31,559
I hope you stay healthy and never fall ill.

734
00:41:32,199 --> 00:41:34,079
I hope many people hold you dear.

735
00:41:34,679 --> 00:41:36,079
Most of all, I hope

736
00:41:36,159 --> 00:41:37,159
you are happy.

737
00:41:42,679 --> 00:41:44,119
Just thinking of those words,

738
00:41:44,199 --> 00:41:46,800
"You can take any of
the fruit on the table,"

739
00:41:47,360 --> 00:41:49,000
they still echo in my ears.

740
00:41:49,719 --> 00:41:51,920
A few mere minutes in time

741
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:54,280
can be an eternity in my memory.

742
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:56,240
So

743
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:58,079
I will love the world you exist in,

744
00:41:58,679 --> 00:41:59,960
take the journeys you've taken,

745
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:02,079
see the sights you've seen,

746
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:04,760
and write the poems you've understood

747
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:07,400
yet left unspoken.

748
00:42:08,519 --> 00:42:09,519
Chen Wan.

749
00:43:25,719 --> 00:43:27,359
Why did you suddenly want to go by water?

750
00:43:28,559 --> 00:43:30,559
Didn't you say you wanted
to go to Feiling Island?

751
00:43:31,119 --> 00:43:32,119
You still remember.

752
00:43:35,119 --> 00:43:35,959
Mr. Zhao, Mr. Chen,

753
00:43:36,039 --> 00:43:37,360
your boat is ready.

754
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:39,240
Would you two like to board now?

755
00:43:39,320 --> 00:43:40,520
Is this a new boat you bought?

756
00:43:41,239 --> 00:43:41,719
No.

757
00:43:42,239 --> 00:43:43,280
This is our boat.

758
00:43:46,679 --> 00:43:48,199
Let's go aboard and take a look first.

759
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:50,440
Right this way.

760
00:43:58,079 --> 00:43:58,999
It's gorgeous.

761
00:43:59,079 --> 00:44:00,079
Thank you.

762
00:44:07,079 --> 00:44:08,639
This is a model of the ship.

763
00:44:08,719 --> 00:44:10,360
I had the designer make a new one

764
00:44:11,559 --> 00:44:13,599
to keep in my office.

765
00:44:13,679 --> 00:44:15,680
You can think of a name for it.

766
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:17,599
I'll have someone paint it on later.

767
00:44:18,960 --> 00:44:20,120
Since you're giving it to me,

768
00:44:21,079 --> 00:44:22,079
you should name it.

769
00:44:23,400 --> 00:44:24,159
Then let's call it

770
00:44:24,239 --> 00:44:24,999
the Keats.

771
00:44:25,079 --> 00:44:26,079
How does that sound?

772
00:44:26,599 --> 00:44:27,880
Sounds great.

773
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:29,320
Later on, we'll have the Keats

774
00:44:29,400 --> 00:44:31,720
make the maiden voyage after
Lai Chi Wun's transformation.

775
00:44:33,559 --> 00:44:36,000
Back when the Lai Chi Wun
Pier project was first launched,

776
00:44:36,920 --> 00:44:37,840
I did daydream about

777
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:39,239
owning a boat myself

778
00:44:40,159 --> 00:44:41,799
and claiming Lai Chi Wun's maiden voyage.

779
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:44,280
Back then, it felt like
pure wishful thinking.

780
00:44:44,840 --> 00:44:45,840
But now...

781
00:44:46,519 --> 00:44:48,360
You decide the route for the maiden voyage.

782
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:49,680
We

783
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:51,039
can spend our honeymoon at sea.

784
00:44:51,920 --> 00:44:52,920
What do you think,

785
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:56,960
Chen Wan?

786
00:44:58,119 --> 00:44:59,119
Spend our what?

787
00:45:00,119 --> 00:45:01,480
You heard what I said.

788
00:45:03,119 --> 00:45:04,599
Didn't you refuse to make it official

789
00:45:05,920 --> 00:45:07,400
because you still wanted to court me?

790
00:45:07,519 --> 00:45:09,279
I can keep courting
you after we're married.

791
00:45:15,079 --> 00:45:15,920
Okay.

792
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:17,000
Sounds good.

793
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:32,439
Chen Wan,

794
00:45:32,519 --> 00:45:33,880
take a look.

795
00:45:33,960 --> 00:45:34,760
In the blueprints,

796
00:45:34,840 --> 00:45:36,480
we can change anything you don't like.

797
00:45:39,159 --> 00:45:41,200
This is a bowling alley.

798
00:45:41,280 --> 00:45:43,119
I get the feeling you quite enjoy bowling.

799
00:45:44,599 --> 00:45:45,639
Over here

800
00:45:45,719 --> 00:45:47,200
is the observation deck for fishing.

801
00:45:47,280 --> 00:45:48,736
When the time comes,
I'll put up a Christmas tree.

802
00:45:48,760 --> 00:45:49,880
When we head out to sea,

803
00:45:49,960 --> 00:45:50,960
you can fish right here.

804
00:45:51,960 --> 00:45:54,119
We can also put a lounge chair right here

805
00:45:54,199 --> 00:45:55,760
so you can nap beside me.

806
00:45:56,960 --> 00:45:57,840
Oh, right.

807
00:45:57,920 --> 00:45:59,119
This is the bar.

808
00:45:59,199 --> 00:46:00,495
Once I pick out the wine cabinets,

809
00:46:00,519 --> 00:46:01,519
you can pick the drinks.

810
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:04,400
Okay.

811
00:46:05,360 --> 00:46:05,840
Thanks.

812
00:46:05,920 --> 00:46:08,296
I've note down the custom trips for the yacht.

813
00:46:08,319 --> 00:46:10,399
Everything will be done before we cast off.

814
00:46:10,480 --> 00:46:11,480
Perfect.

815
00:46:13,559 --> 00:46:15,999
When did you go see the designer?

816
00:46:16,079 --> 00:46:16,720
I

817
00:46:16,800 --> 00:46:18,479
went before the roadshow.

818
00:46:18,559 --> 00:46:19,599
Looks like you're

819
00:46:19,679 --> 00:46:21,439
still keeping a lot of things

820
00:46:21,519 --> 00:46:22,519
from me.

821
00:46:25,000 --> 00:46:26,000
There's nothing else.

822
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:31,119
Sorry, let me take this call.

823
00:46:32,679 --> 00:46:33,159
Hello?

824
00:46:33,239 --> 00:46:34,239
What is it?

825
00:46:36,159 --> 00:46:37,159
Good man.

826
00:46:38,519 --> 00:46:39,599
I'm not.

827
00:46:39,679 --> 00:46:40,920
Chen Wan is.

828
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:42,280
Everything I've done

829
00:46:42,880 --> 00:46:44,960
doesn't even come close to
how good he's been to me.

830
00:46:54,840 --> 00:46:56,120
We've arrived at Feiling Island.

831
00:46:57,679 --> 00:46:59,039
We should've come a long time ago.

832
00:47:04,039 --> 00:47:05,599
Sometimes, looking at the ocean,

833
00:47:06,559 --> 00:47:08,519
makes you feel how truly tiny humans are,

834
00:47:09,159 --> 00:47:11,599
and how little is actually up to us.

835
00:47:11,679 --> 00:47:13,159
Even a massive project

836
00:47:13,239 --> 00:47:14,680
like the Full Moon Channel

837
00:47:14,760 --> 00:47:15,479
is really nothing more than

838
00:47:15,559 --> 00:47:17,800
a drop in the ocean
amid the shifting stars.

839
00:47:21,159 --> 00:47:22,280
Then take hold of the things

840
